  "question": {
    "text": "A radioactive nucleus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> with a half-life <math><mi>T</mi></math>, decays into a nucleus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. At <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, there is no nucleus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. At some time&nbsp;<math><mi>t</mi></math>, the ratio of the number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> to that of <math><mi>A</mi></math> is <math><mn>0</mn><mtext>.</mtext><mn>3</mn></math>. Then, <math><mi>t</mi></math> is given by: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mtext>Consider</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wrjiM",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>1.3</mn></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MoZLq",
      "text": "<math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi> </mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi> </mi><mn>1.3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "kIiJb",
      "text": "<math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>1.3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></math>",
